# Promoted from `.scratch/cloud-phase/spike-11/Dockerfile.dockerignore`, then tightened by ticket
# 07's first real leak scan over the built image — which found two things this file did not
# exclude. Both are recorded here rather than silently fixed, because the next `COPY . .` will
# reintroduce whatever this file forgets.

# `node_modules` is installed from the committed lockfile inside the image. Copying the host's
# tree in would carry Windows-resolved binaries into a Linux image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# **Found by the leak scan:** `services/agents/.venv` is a 130 MB Python virtualenv built on the
# host, and `COPY . .` was putting it in the image — Windows-built artifacts in a Linux image,
# carrying `cacert.pem` files the scan correctly flagged as credential-shaped.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# **Found by the leak scan:** the test suite was in the image. It is not needed to run the service,
# it is where every fixture secret lives, and an image that carries its own tests has a larger
# readable surface than the thing it deploys.
**/tests
**/*.test.ts

# **Found by ticket 07's deploy wizard**, whose stage 3 warned about an uncommitted `.gitignore` on
# every run. `.dockerignore` governs the build context and `.gitignore` does not, so the file is
# inert in a production runtime — but nothing here excluded it, `COPY . .` carried it in, and every
# edit to it therefore changed the image bytes. The warning was technically true, useless in
# practice, and firing at the one prompt that asks the operator to judge whether the tag is honest.
.gitignore
.gitattributes
# This file too. Docker reads it from the context root before the context is assembled, so
# excluding it still applies it — it just stops it being copied into the runtime, where it is the
# same inert cargo as the two above and would recreate the same false alarm from a different file.
.dockerignore

# Operator-side only. `scripts/` is the two cloud wizards and the volume conformance harness; all
# three run on the machine doing the deploying and none is reachable from inside the container.
# `deploy/` is the exception that must stay, because `docker-entrypoint.sh` is this image's
# ENTRYPOINT — so the four files in it that the image never reads are excluded by name rather than
# by excluding the directory. `container-smoke.mjs` and `image-leak-scan.mjs` are `docker cp`'d in
# at the moment they run and are never read from `/app`; `fetch-service-env.sh` runs on the COS
# host, not in the container.
scripts
deploy/README.md
deploy/cloud-init.yaml
deploy/fetch-service-env.sh
deploy/container-smoke.mjs
deploy/image-leak-scan.mjs

.git
.github
.scratch
dist
**/dist
out
**/out
docs

# Never, under any circumstances.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key
credentials.json
service-account.json
.npmrc
.netrc
